Here's the CartComponent:

```jsx
import React from'react';
import { useSelector, useDispatch } from'react-redux';
import { addItem, removeItem } from './cartSlice';
import { CheckoutButton } from './CheckoutButton';

const CartComponent = () => {
  const { items } = useSelector((state) => state.cart);
  const dispatch = useDispatch();

  const handleAddItem = (item) => {
    dispatch(addItem(item));
  };

  const handleRemoveItem = (id) => {
    dispatch(removeItem(id));
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Shopping Cart</h2>
      <ul>
        {items.map((item) => (
          <li key={item.id}>
            <span>{item.name}</span>
            <span>Quantity: {item.quantity}</span>
            <button onClick={() => handleRemoveItem(item.id)}>Remove</button>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <CheckoutButton />
      <span>Total: {items.reduce((acc, curr) => acc + curr.price * curr.quantity, 0)}</span>
    </div>
  );
};

export default CartComponent;
```

This component assumes you have a `CheckoutButton` component that you'll need to implement separately. 

The `handleAddItem` function calls the `addItem` action creator with the item to add, and the `handleRemoveItem` function calls the `removeItem` action creator with the ID of the item to remove. 

This component also uses the `useReducer` hook from Redux Toolkit to get the `items` from the Redux state and to dispatch actions to update the state. 

The `CheckoutButton` component should handle the checkout logic when clicked. 

Here's a simple implementation of the `CheckoutButton`:

```jsx
import React from'react';
import { useHistory } from'react-router-dom';

const CheckoutButton = () => {
  const history = useHistory();

  const handleCheckout = () => {
    history.push('/checkout');
  };

  return (
    <button onClick={handleCheckout}>Checkout</button>
  );
};

export default CheckoutButton;
```

This button simply redirects the user to the checkout page when clicked. You'll need to implement the checkout page separately. 

Note: This code assumes you have already set up Redux Toolkit and the Redux store in your application.

